defect c7-III-02LC-machine-header D10 maps:src:D.2.36 Remove the machine status/dependency header and print the small theorem tag; all permanent identities are preserved.
defect c7-III-02LC-local-assignment D27 maps:src:D.2.36 Refined statement retains maps:src:D.2.36 and D.OP1. Prescribed-fan normal weights are +/-nu at the cusp and +/-w at I_p. The exact integral invariant is mathfrak p=((b/p-a nu)/2)s, zero exactly when w^2=nu^2. Pattern 21 (OS56,2,5,I3 zero,e=1) has w=2 but actual refined class zero from p1 pairing -50=0 mod5. Pattern 30 (OS56/III,1,10,I3 zero,m=4,e=1,n=3,r0=0) has w=4 but actual refined class 2s from pairing -22=3 mod 5. A unit automorphism cannot exchange zero and nonzero. Exactly ten assignments change; type counts two and one stand.
defect c7-III-02LC-physical-wall D25 maps:eq:D.OP6 The old polynomial identity is algebraically correct, but the four untransformed physical vertices are not the prescribed short-fan wall in general. The explicit C0 map and inverse give psi_ph(C0 t)=-t^tKt+a(nu t1-br t2); its actual wall is -2a(nu+br) and complex line degree +2a(nu+br). All physical support differences and unit factors are retained; D.OP6 is refined under the same identity.
defect c7-III-02LC-normal-weight-normalization D25 maps:src:D.2.36 The physical cusp chart has weights +/-nu. The subgroup map exponent nu^-1, with inverse nu, changes both local pairs to +/-1 and +/-w/nu. D.OP9 and D.OP10 retain their identities with the corrected denominators; the original u[C]=1 normalization has pairing -2(1-w^2/nu^2).
defect c7-III-02LC-global-line-isomorphism D22 maps:src:D.2.36 Give the complete Gaussian gauge, its reciprocal, and z^a with inverse z^-a. They recover the literal original h,F,J maps, every inverse and all unit functions. Their scalar-invariant overlap composites identify the single global real line exactly, including swept cycles and scalar lift; no fibrewise-only comparison is used.
defect c7-III-02LC-rank-one-extension D22 maps:src:D.2.36 Supply primitive short and long matrices and their inverses, original-germ/unit/collar transport, full nonsymmetric pairing Gaussian gauge, and rank-one support differences for alpha>1 and beta=0. All 96 occurrences and the 24 nonprimitive-H occurrences are verified after exposure. The original support identity and I_p primitive-period conclusion stand.
defect c7-III-02LC-global-borel-shift D22 maps:src:D.2.36 Choose a whole-circle-fixed endpoint, prove the split fundamental group and unique order-p subgroup, and compute the complete degree-two restriction kernel. A single global t shift with its inverse removes the common character while retaining eta H1(E). This resolves the global comparison at its actual scope.
defect c7-III-02LC-full-invariant-maps D22 maps:src:D.2.36 Keep the full CP3 generator detector and inverse, the marked classifying map, the integral H4 reduction isomorphism, and exact quarter-Pontryagin map. The final classification uses marked Theorems 3 and 5 with the Section 4.1 uniqueness map and its induced H2 inverse, not homology alone.
defect c7-III-02LC-historical-computation D09 maps:src:D.2.36 Replace the historical execution/certificate assertion by the explicit factor/component/option enumeration and complete 36-pattern table. The newly written raw-fixture computation is separately recorded; the historical target program and output remain unopened and uncredited.
defect c7-III-02LC-primary-locators D18 maps:src:D.2.36 Use complete marked Theorem 3 p.795, Theorem 5 p.796 and the actual Section 4.1 proof p.809, together with the quarter-map and Section 3.13 definition. The admitted bounded K9 source-description correction is retained; both LC free ranks vanish. No claim that printed p.793 says H3 and no whole-PDF credit is made.
event publish:c7:III:02LC:targeted targeted proof check group=publish:c7:III:02LC Complete pre-exposure derivation frozen 2026-11-25T02:16:02.099240+00:00 and fully root-reviewed before release. Reconstructed all 172 natural rows and 36 minimal patterns on 30 rows from the defining fixture, with every finite order and free simply connected twist. Derived actual original-period maps/inverses, prescribed-fan Cp fixed data, a single global equivariant line and Borel character comparison, full integral mu=0, PD p1=2(b/p-a nu)s and mathfrak p=((b/p-a nu)/2)s. Proved exact Tate conversion, all generator/action inverses and full oriented classification. Entire 474-line new program and 690-line output read, including all 36 raw patterns, ten changed assignments and 432 marked diffeomorphism H2 maps/inverses. The counts remain two order-five types and one order-seven type; every realization is an actual constructed member. Exact input, primary and exposure scopes are recorded. All six fresh hashes are unchanged. No historical target execution, extra independent-family count, canonical/global mutation, current-PDF build/reading, unit closure or publication-gate credit. Root admission pending.
event publish:c7:III:02LC:assignment-refuted refuted, with the refined statement's id group=publish:c7:III:02LC D27: refutes the local w^2=1 assignment in maps:src:D.2.36; refined statement retains maps:src:D.2.36, D.OP1 and all permanent identities. The corrected full formula is H2=H3=Z/p, b3=0, spin, mu=0, PD p1=2(b/p-a nu)s, mathfrak p=((b/p-a nu)/2)s and P=(b/p)/2(1-nu^2/w^2); zero iff w^2=nu^2. OS56(2,5), I3 zero, e=1 gives w=2 but actual P=0 from pairing -50=0 mod 5; OS56/III(1,10), I3 zero, m=4,e=1,n=3,r0=0 gives w=4 but actual P=2 from pairing -22=3 mod 5. Exact unit marking maps cannot interchange zero/nonzero. Ten assignments 21,22,25,26,27,28,29,30,33,34 change; the zero list is 21,22,25,26,27,28,29,33, with P30=2 and P34=3. The two/one type counts and mu=0 stand.  Exact input, primary and exposure scopes are recorded. All six fresh hashes are unchanged. No historical target execution, extra independent-family count, canonical/global mutation, current-PDF build/reading, unit closure or publication-gate credit. Root admission pending.
event publish:c7:III:02LC:fan-and-action-refuted refuted, with the refined statement's id group=publish:c7:III:02LC D25: refutes only the physical-wall identification and inconsistent normal-weight normalization in the proof of maps:src:D.2.36. Refined intermediate identities retain maps:eq:D.OP5, maps:eq:D.OP6, maps:eq:D.OP9 and maps:eq:D.OP10. The exact period map C0=[[nu,-br],[ar,rho]], inverse [[rho,br],[-ar,nu]], gives psi_ph(C0 t)=-t^tKt+a(nu t1-br t2); the actual prescribed wall is -2a(nu+br) and positive complex line degree +2a(nu+br). The physical cusp weights are +/-nu, while the subgroup map exponent nu^-1 with inverse nu gives cusp +/-1 and elliptic +/-w/nu. Thus the corrected localization is alpha_C/nu^2+alpha_E/w^2=0; in u_C[C]=1 marking its pairing is -2(1-w^2/nu^2). True original h,F,J and rank-one support identities are retained through explicit gauges and inverses.  Exact input, primary and exposure scopes are recorded. All six fresh hashes are unchanged. No historical target execution, extra independent-family count, canonical/global mutation, current-PDF build/reading, unit closure or publication-gate credit. Root admission pending.
